PATCH 407: FUN_0000_6980 voxel raycaster -- apply the map-load SMC to the colormap-read
displacement + the coord shift (the ported decompile froze the STATIC image constants).

At map-load the block 0x8a7f-0x8b29 self-modifies ~30 slots across the voxel render fns:
[0x8490] (the LOD, =11 for the AZER1 2048^2 map) is written into every shld/shift-amount
slot, and [0x8498] (the HM size, =0x400000) into every colormap-read displacement slot.
Ghidra decompiled 6980 with the UN-patched image values (shld $0xa=10; colormap disp
0x100000), so the port read the colormap at [0x85bc]+0x100000 (a DARK buffer INSIDE the
2048^2 HM) instead of [0x85bc]+0x400000 = [0x85b8] (the LIGHT terrain colormap), and
indexed a 1024^2-strided map instead of 2048^2.  ORACLE-PROVEN: the 6b1a displacement
reads 0x100000 in the static image but 0x400000 in the dosbox-fist render-time guest-RAM
dump (SMC 8b24: mov [0x8498],0x6b1d).  Correcting 6980 to use the SMC sources DAT_0000_8490
(shift) + DAT_0000_8498 (colormap displacement) matches the original's render-time code.

MEASURED (real 2048^2 buffers): terrain index match 10.6% (baseline) -> 78.7% vs the
oracle 9200 framematched render -- a 7.5x improvement, root-caused + oracle-proven.
6980 runs only on the mission windshield path (not the 159 verify flows -> no regression;
verify.sh both stays 159/0 native==wasm).  The sibling voxel fns (6d/7f/8f/90 for ops
0x10 etc.) carry the same SMC slots and get the same correction in follow-up patches.
